    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15854" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ē-nŭmĕrātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		enumero, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a counting up</i>, <i>enumerating.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">malorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Leg. 3, 10</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bonorum et malorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Part. Or. 17, 58</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">singulorum argumentorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Clu. 24</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oratorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Brut. 36 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			rhetor. lang., <i>a recapitulation</i> (Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνακεφαλαίωσις</span>), <i><span class="en">Cic. Inv.
				1, 29, 45</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1, 52</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint. 5,
				14, 11</span></i>; <i><span class="en">6, 1,
				1 al.</span></i></div>
